#question(title: [Where is the maximum?])[
  We know the following about the function
  $h$:
  - The domain of $h$ is
    $display((- 4 comma 4))$.
  - $h$ is continuous on its domain.
  - $h$ is differentiable on its domain,
    except at $0$.
  - $h' (x) = 0 quad <==> quad x = - 1 " or " 1$.

  #slide-block(title: [What can you conclude about the maximum of $h$?])[
    + $h$ has a maximum at $x = - 1$, or $1$.
    + $h$ has a maximum at $x = - 1, 0,$ or
      $1$.
    + $h$ has a maximum at
      $x = - 4, - 1, 0, 1,$ or $4$.
    + None of the above.
  ]
]
